# No em dashes in user-facing web copy

Do not use the em dash character (`—`, Unicode U+2014) in text shown to users in the web app: JSX copy, button labels, toasts, placeholders, aria-labels, titles, etc.

Comments, backend code, and internal docs may use em dashes if needed.

Use instead in UI copy:
- A period and new sentence
- A comma
- A colon
- Parentheses
- A hyphen `-` for empty table cells (not an em dash)

Examples:
- Bad: `Complete onboarding — then check progress`
- Good: `Complete onboarding, then check progress`
